NNAAMMEE
     vviiaappmm — VIA SMBus controller and VIA VT82C686A/VT8231 hardware monitor

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     vviiaappmm** aatt ppccii??
     iiiicc** aatt vviiaappmm??

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vviiaappmm driver provides support for the bus control and power manage‐
     ment component of the VIA VT82C596, VT82C596B, VT82C686A, VT8231, VT8233,
     VT8233A, VT8235, VT8237, VT8237A, VT8237S, VT8251, CX700, VX800, VX855
     and VX900 South Bridges.  Only the SMBus host interface is supported and
     can be used with the iic(4) framework.

     The vviiaappmm driver provides support for the hardware monitor in the VIA
     VT82C686A and VT8231 South Bridges.  The hardware monitor is used with
     the sysctl(8) interface.

     The device has 10 sensors:

           SSeennssoorr    UUnniittss    TTyyppiiccaall UUssee
           TSENS1    uK       CPU temperature
           TSENS2    uK       System temperature
           TSENS3    uK       Unknown
           FAN1      RPM      CPU fan
           FAN2      RPM      System fan
           VSENS1    uV DC    CPU core voltage (2.0V)
           VSENS2    uV DC    North Bridge core voltage (2.5V)
           Vcore     uV DC    Internal core voltage (3.3V)
           VSENS3    uV DC    +5V
           VSENS4    uV DC    +12V

     Sensor data is updated every 1.5 seconds.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     iic(4), intro(4), pci(4), sensorsd(8), sysctl(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The vviiaappmm driver first appeared in OpenBSD 3.9.

     The vviiaaeennvv driver first appeared in NetBSD 1.5.  OpenBSD support was
     added in OpenBSD 3.4.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
